#
#   The Behemoth logo (START) -> on the first run only, "No Alien Hominid
#   save games found ... Press A to continue" (A; the save is written) ->
#   main menu, cursor on GAME (A) -> NEW GAME / LOAD LEVEL, cursor on NEW
#   GAME (A) -> a controls picture, "A SKIP" (A) -> the intro cutscene (the
#   ship crash; A does not skip it, it ends by itself in ~24 s) -> level 1,
#   the FBI street, "PLEASE WAIT" -> player control.
#
# The menu presses are an A train 5 s apart: with a save on the disk there
# is no save prompt, the train reaches the cutscene one press early, and
# the spare A presses land in the cutscene, which ignores them.
#
# Player control: LX min walked the alien from the right edge of the street
# to the "WE KILL ALIENS" sign (nav frames 009-moved -> 010-left). The
# play pattern runs both ways, fires (X) and jumps (A). The FBI agents kill
# a blind player in about 20 s a life; after the last life and the
# continue countdown the game returns to the NEW GAME menu, and the
# pattern's A presses start a new game from there (A: NEW GAME, A: skip the
# controls picture, the cutscene plays out), so the soak stays in play.
#
